<%- include('partials/header') %>
    <main>
        <h1>
            <%= title %>
        </h1>
        <h2>Welcome to the CSE 340 Service Network!</h2>
        <p>Our mission is to promote service across the world by connecting volunteers with service opportunities in
            their community.</p>
        <img class="main-logo" src="/images/cse340-service-network.png" alt="CSE 340 Service Network Logo">

        <%# PLAIN ENGLISH: Show a "My Dashboard" link, but only to people who are logged in.
            LOGIC: The logged-in value comes from res.locals (set for every page, the same
                   value the header uses for Logout vs. Register/Login). True = show the
                   link. False = the link is left out of the page completely.
            WHY WE NEED IT: Gives logged-in users an easy way to reach their dashboard.
            LEARNING GAP: This only hides the link. It does NOT protect the page. Someone
                          could still type /dashboard in the address bar. The real
                          protection is the lock (requireLogin) in the /dashboard route. %>
        <% if (isLoggedIn) { %>
            <p><a href="/dashboard">My Dashboard</a></p>
        <% } %>
    </main>
    <%- include('partials/footer') %>
